<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Consol interim shr slips, no div.</title>
<headline>Consol interim shr slips, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)	157.6	 vs    187.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   101.42	 vs    120.35</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   124.95	 vs    165.30</p>
<p>    Tax			  23.20	 vs    44.83</p>
<p>    Finance costs	    56.72	 vs    43.55</p>
<p>    Turnover		1,784.60	 vs    1,688.50</p>
<p>    Share of associates'    0.34	 vs    0.11</p>
<p>Full name: Consol Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said with the disposal of its rubber business from this year, it would become a focused packaging company.</p>
<p>It said the economy continued to perform at a dissapointing level and earnings for the full year were unlikely to improve significantly upon the trend reflected during this period.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
